
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## On-device connection setup check

1. Flash the firmware. If no profile has been saved, the connection editor opens.
2. Enter the Wi-Fi network, optional Wi-Fi password, DCC-EX Command Station IP
   address, and port, then choose **Save & Connect**.
3. Confirm the bottom status button progresses through Wi-Fi and DCC-EX
   connection states, then shows **DCC-EX CONNECTED**.
4. Tap that status button, edit a value if needed, and save it again.
5. Restart the throttle and confirm it reconnects using the saved profile.

## On-device display settings check

1. Open the connection editor from the connection-status button and choose
   **Display**. The control is also available during first-time connection setup.
2. Adjust brightness and confirm the backlight changes immediately.
3. Select a sleep timeout, wait for the selected idle period, and confirm the
   backlight turns off. Turn the encoder or press the physical button to wake it.
4. Restart the throttle and confirm both display settings were retained.
